// src/parse/parse.zen
//
// The parser's whole surface, in one file of starred re-exports.
// A folder root is its folder's public surface and nothing else, so
// every name a consumer can reach through `parse` is listed here, and
// anything absent is module-private on purpose: the bounded scans, the
// poison builders and the seven-way `value_shape` fork are the
// parser's own business and no caller has any use for them.
//
// WHAT A CONSUMER ACTUALLY NEEDS is four names. Build a `Parser` over a
// token stream, call `module`, read the tree and the diagnostics back
// off it:
//
//     p ::= alloc.Parser(tokens, "src/main.zen");
//     m = p.module("main").try();
//     p.diags.len.match({ .. });      // rejected, or not
//     p.tree                          // every node m refers to
//
// The tree is read back off the Parser rather than returned beside the
// module because an `Ast` owns `Vec`s: a copy of one diverges from the
// original the first time either grows, so there is exactly one and
// the Parser holds it.

// what a parse produces, and what it produces instead when it fails
Diag*, Note*, diag*, diag_at* = parse.parse_diag

// what a parse consumes. PROVISIONAL — `src/lex/lex.zen` owns this
// alphabet and this line becomes `Token*, TokenKind* = lex.lex` the
// day it lands. See parse_token.zen's header for the three assumptions
// the parser was written against.
Token*, TokenKind* = parse.parse_token

// the machine, and the one budget it enforces
Parser*, Mark*, MAX_DEPTH* = parse.parser

// the entry point, and the pieces a consumer that is not parsing a
// whole file might want: `zen fmt` reads a module, an LSP completion
// re-parses one expression, and a test builds one type.
module*, declaration* = parse.parse_decl
block* = parse.parse_stmt
expr* = parse.parse_expr
type* = parse.parse_type
pattern* = parse.parse_pattern
arms* = parse.parse_match
